OS designer can minimize the amount of operating system code that runs in supervisor mode, and execute the bulk of the operating system in user mode. This kernel organization is called a microkernel.

From this book's perspective, microkernel and monolithic operating system share many key ideas. they implemenmt system calls, they use page tables, they handle interrupts, they support processes, they use locks for concurrency control, they implement a file system, etc.

the xv6 kernel source is in the kernel/ sub-directory

